From 138d88bba3ac11c7e226d44aa82aa581cd8b1cb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:26:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban pacing: read-only views describe a paced pool
 as a hold only with pace_starts

Review of 262b95542d: paced_pools still returned a paced pool under the
default, so the priority-raise guard refused "held by llm_pacing" and the
chat-wait / parent-unclaimed notices named a pacing hold that no dispatcher
makes. It now counts paced only with pace_starts (held always).

The notice and priority-guard test files describe the opt-in mode and say
so (an autouse fixture); test_kanban_pacing_default_reads.py covers each
consumer on the default config. kanban.md says the token throttle is a
separate component and what a paced pool does without it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
